Average HBW trip length moves in the intended direction in every county — the most direct measure of the mechanism working as intended.

### Trip Length Distribution {#trip-length-distribution}

The average above is one number; the full distribution shows *how* the shift happens — built directly from the origin-destination trip matrix and distance skim (region-wide, all HBW trips regardless of mode, in 2-mile bins), not the production-side estimate used for the average. The baseline curve is shown alongside whichever shift level is selected. This is the single most direct visual confirmation that the per-origin tilt mechanism did what it was designed to do.

